{"name":"Light Bassinet","hex":"#ded0d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"bassinet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A newborn baby's bed, traditionally woven with reeds or straw; a (wicker) cradle."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of bascinet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bassinet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bassinet","blocks":[{"text":"A bassinet, bassinette, or cradle is a bed specifically for babies from birth to about four months. Bassinets are generally designed to work with fixed legs or caster wheels, while cradles are generally designed to provide a rocking or gliding motion. Bassinets and cradles are distinguished from Moses baskets and carry cots, which are designed to be carried and sit directly on the floor or furniture. After four months, babies are often transferred to a crib or cot. In the United States, however, the bedside sleeper is the prevalent option, since they are generally bigger, recommended up to 6 months, and often used up to a year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Walraversijde50.jpg/330px-Walraversijde50.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bassinet","wikidata":"Q1131270"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Bassinet.JPG/500px-Bassinet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Bassinet.JPG/500px-Bassinet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Movable, but not portable, home bassinet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABassinet.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/HRBassinet.JPG/500px-HRBassinet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/HRBassinet.JPG/1280px-HRBassinet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/HRBassinet.JPG/500px-HRBassinet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rooming-in bassinet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHRBassinet.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Indian_cradle.jpg/500px-Indian_cradle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Indian_cradle.jpg/1280px-Indian_cradle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Indian_cradle.jpg/500px-Indian_c